in the aftermath of the Battle of  Winterfell beyond the thousands of men  left dead and injured allegiances have  shifted alliances have changed and of  course there's still another war to  fight Cersei is still waiting and her  army is ready to attack Daenerys John  and their allied forces with just a  handful of episodes remaining in the  final season there's plenty left to  accomplish between the quest for the  throne as well as another war so here's  everything you need to know about the  last of the starts the fourth episode of  the last season of Game of Thrones as  you might expect after the carnage of  the Battle of Winterfell the last of the  starts opens with a slow and emotional  funeral sequence characters like  Daenerys and Sansa are given the chance  to mourn loved ones including Jorah  Mormont and fian Greyjoy who gave their  lives during the battle after a moving  speech by John the entire crew retires  to the Great Hall of Winterfell to  celebrate their victory giving the  characters as well as the audience a  brief respite from the violence and  sadness during the celebration Daenerys  takes a moment to win some more brownie  points with the northerners by naming  ginjury Robert Baratheon's illegitimate  son and sole remaining heir as the Lord  of storms in encouraged by his new title  and still stuck on his one night with  Arya Gendry rushes off to propose to his  ladylove only to be gently yet firmly  rebuffed arya definitely isn't looking  to get wiped up anytime soon and being  the lady of a grand castle probably  isn't quite as appealing as stealing  faces and killing enemies so  unfortunately for ginjury he'll probably  have to find a different lady to help  run his castle at this point it's  looking like robert's dream of joining  the Baratheon and Stark houses may not  come true after all  ever since she travelled with the  Kingslayer several seasons ago and saw  his fall from celebrated night to  one-handed enemy of Queen Cersei Brienne  has clearly had feelings for Jaime and  it certainly seems as if he returned to  those feelings from the time he saved  her from a bear pit to the moment he  dubbed her the first female Knight of  the Seven Kingdoms  after Tyrion shrewdly reveals that  Brienne is a virgin during a drinking  game the formidable fighter is  uncharacteristically embarrassed but  once Jaime comes to comfort her she gets  over that embarrassment pretty quickly  Jaime however has to choose where his  allegiances lie despite his seemingly  close relationship with both Tyrion and  Brienne he ends up heading right back to  Cersei as he leaves in the middle of the  night Brienne rush  to bring him back to the northern side  but he insists he's really just as  hateful as a sister and leaves her  heartbroken a Lannister always pays his  debts but which scores will Jamie be  hoping to settle when he gets back to  King's Landing the news that Jon Snow  isn't Ned Stark's bastard at all but the  legitimate son of Prince Rhaegar  Targaryen and Ned's sister Liana has  been out in the open for viewers since  season seven  when bran and Sam discovered the truth  about his secret royal lineage as the  person with the strongest claim to the  Iron Throne Jon has unwittingly made  himself an enemy of just about everyone  on the show especially his new  girlfriend Daenerys who is also his aunt  in case all of this needed to get  weirder and worse even though Daenerys  begs Jon not to tell his sisters about  his real parentage John can't help  himself  swearing both Arya and Sansa to secrecy  as he spills the beans about his royal  blood despite her vow  Sansa quickly tells her former husband  Tyrion about who John really is and  naturally he immediately tells the  secret to Varys with information this  important it was always impossible that  characters wouldn't find out but this  turn of events is bad news for both John  and Daenerys who both stand to lose a  lot the minute the truth of his lineage  truly goes public despite the recent  victory against the army of the dead  Daenerys is more on edge than ever even  during the post battle celebration at  Winterfell where she finds herself  isolated from the crowd and left to  wander off alone seemingly angry at her  failure to make friends among the  northerners by the end of the episode  Daenerys has faced two massive losses  both pushing her to her absolute  breaking point not only does she lose  ships and cavalry during a surprise  attack on her fleet courtesy of euron  greyjoy  and Cersei Lannister ZAR me she loses  her Ragle  who becomes the first of her dragons to  be killed by humans with the aid of  massive ballistas known as scorpions in  the aftermath her best friend and  confidant miss on day ends up captured  by the enemy and when Daenerys and her  team offers Cersei her life in exchange  for her surrender Cersei has Musante  beheaded in front of them another cruel  show of power from a monarch who knows  how to prove a brutal point after losing  Jorah regal and miss on day in quick  succession  Daenerys might be on the brink of  succumbing to the madness that  runs in her family even though Daenerys  constantly says she wants to avoid  becoming her father the Mad King these  tragedies all point to her reaching a  breaking point before long especially as  this war continues to push her to her  limit meanwhile Cersei has long been one  of the most brutal characters on the  show and despite Tyrians pleas for  humanity and peace she's not changing  anytime soon for the moment it appears  that her ruthless streak is still  serving her well against her more nobly  intentioned enemies will her commitment  to cruelty be the difference-maker in  the coming war against Daenerys or will  it be her undoing check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos about Game of Thrones are  coming soon subscribe to our YouTube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]
 

